# Cin7 architecture (ContainerDoor OMS)

## Principle
OMS domain = **Operational Line Items** (A/B/C…), never “Shopify order as the unit of fulfilment”.

```
Operational Line Item → Integration adapter → External system
```

Monday already follows this (one pulse per line). **Cin7 must too.**

## Preferred mapping
```
Shopify #1001
  Line A → Monday pulse A → Cin7 Sales Order A
  Line B → Monday pulse B → Cin7 Sales Order B
  Line C → Monday pulse C → Cin7 Sales Order C
```

## Cin7 API validation (Omni v1 SalesOrders)

| Question | Answer |
|----------|--------|
| Can we create one SO per operational line? | **Yes.** `POST /v1/SalesOrders` accepts an array; each object is an independent Sales Order. |
| API limitation that forces one SO per Shopify order? | **None found.** |
| Why split anyway? | Cin7 has **one `trackingCode` per Sales Order** (max 50). One SO for multi-line OMS breaks independent tracking/dispatch. |
| Can multiple SOs reference same Shopify order? | **Yes.** Use shared `customerOrderNo` = Shopify order name (`#CDL215347`). Unique `reference` per line (max **30** chars) e.g. `#CDL215347A` (same as Monday pulse name). |
| Relationship keys | Shopify `orderId` + `variantId` → OMS line ops → `mondayItemId` + `cin7SalesOrderId` |

Other useful fields: `logisticsCarrier`, `estimatedDeliveryDate`, `internalComments`, `deliveryInstructions`, `freightDescription`. No first-class “freight ref” field — put consignment ref in `freightDescription` / comments / custom field if needed later.

## Adapter (do not hardcode grouping in OMS)
- Module: `app/lib/cin7-adapter.server.ts`
- Env: `CIN7_SO_STRATEGY=per_line` (default) | `grouped` (legacy only)
- Helpers: `buildCin7SalesOrderReference`, `buildCin7CustomerOrderNo`, `resolveCin7SalesOrderId`, `saveCin7LineLink`
- **Resolve order:** line `cin7SalesOrderId` first → fall back to order-level legacy id
- Changing strategy later = adapter + create path only; OMS line-item CRUD stays unchanged

## Schema
| Location | Field | Role |
|----------|-------|------|
| `OrderLineItemOperationalData` | `cin7SalesOrderId` | **Canonical** Cin7 SO id for the line |
| same | `cin7SalesOrderCode` | Cin7 returned `code` |
| same | `cin7SalesOrderRef` | Our `reference` sent on create |
| `OrderOperationalData` | `cin7SalesOrderId` | **Legacy** grouped SO / “any link” mirror — do not use as source of truth for line sync |

## Current code debt (migrate toward adapter)
- Webhook `createCin7EntryForOrder` still creates **one grouped** SO (all SKUs) + writes order-level id only.
- `api.cin7-create`, `api.cin7-update`, `api.cin7-status`, `sync-middleware`, `api.order-status` still resolve order-level id (middleware should use `resolveCin7SalesOrderId`).
- `extractCarrierFromOrder` broken (returns shipping title) — fix when touching create.
- Notes / bulk Cin7 UI still Coming Soon.

## Implementation order
1. Schema meta fields + adapter + `resolveCin7SalesOrderId` everywhere (sync/status/update).
2. Webhook + `/api/cin7-create`: create **per freight line** SO; store on line ops; `customerOrderNo` = order name; `reference` = `#OrderLetter`.
3. Status/diff/update per line against that line’s SO.
4. Enable notes → `appendCin7InternalComment` on **line** SO.
5. Legacy: keep reading order-level id until backfill; optional backfill script later.
6. Never teach OMS UI to edit “the order’s Cin7 id” as the operational unit.

## Auth / env
`CIN7_USERNAME` + `CIN7_SYNC_TOKEN` (Basic) + `CIN7_SYNC_URL` or `CIN7_BASE_URL` + optional `CIN7_SO_STRATEGY`.
